# Feature / phase shipped — update docs

When you **finish implementing** a spec feature, close an implementation **phase**, or move something from *planned* to *shipped*, update every place that still describes it as future work. Do not mark the task done until this pass is complete (in addition to [`changelog.mdc`](changelog.mdc)).

## Trigger

Apply this rule when any of the following become true in code:

- A phase in `docs/en|tr/11-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (or a feature doc § “Implementation plan”) is complete
- A spec section marked **planned / planlandı / gelecek / optional phase** is now live
- OpenAPI, migrations, operator UI, or SDK surface for a documented capability lands

## Required doc sync

| Area | Update |
|------|--------|
| Feature spec (e.g. `docs/en|tr/16-*.md`) | Status → **implemented / shipped**; phase checklist `- [ ]` → `- [x]`; acceptance criteria checked |
| `docs/en|tr/11-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` | Phase table **done**; optional items checked if shipped; remove stale “known limitations” |
| Cross-cutting spec | `07-SERVER-CONFIGURATION`, `08-SECURITY`, `10-DATA-MODEL`, `12-ERROR-CODES` — drop “planned” headers; describe current behaviour |
| Index | `docs/README.md`, `docs/en|tr/README.md` — reading-order table, version history, spec metadata |
| Operator | `docs/OPERATOR.md` — env vars, UI, admin routes for the feature |
| API SSOT | Root `openapi.yaml` (+ `docs/openapi.yaml` if kept in sync) |
| Web / agents | `apps/web/messages`, guides pages, `public/agents/*.md`, `public/llms.txt`, Postman artifacts when API or env docs change |
| Package pointers | `packages/*/TODO.md`, root `README.md` links if paths or scope changed |
| Changelog | Root + affected package `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` |

Update **both** `docs/en/` and `docs/tr/` when the spec exists in both languages.

## Wording rules

- Replace **planned / planlandı / Planlanıyor / gelecek faz / to be implemented** with **shipped / yayında / implemented** only when the capability is actually in the repo (tests or UI verify).
- Leave future-only items explicit (e.g. S3 blob, Stripe webhook, v1.4 attestation) — do not mark them shipped.
- Prefer **relative links** inside `docs/en/` and `docs/tr/` (`../openapi.yaml`, `../OPERATOR.md`), not repo-root `docs/...` paths.
- Phase checklists: mark items `[x]` when done; do not delete historical phase headings.

## Quick verification

Before finishing, search markdown (and agent docs) for stale future tense:

```
planlandı|planned|Planlanıyor|geliştirilecek|to be implemented|— planned|— planlandı
```

Fix or justify every hit tied to the shipped scope.

## Example (app registry v1.3)

```
# Before
**v1.3.0 (planned):** Application registry …
## Application registry (v1.3 — planned)

# After
**v1.3.0 (shipped):** Application registry …
## Application registry (v1.3 — shipped)
```

Also check: `16-APP-REGISTRY.md` §20 checklists, `OPERATOR.md` “Faz 8…” headings, README spec version row.
